# Contribute

Import UiSite from "../src/ui_site.lg".
Import WebBoard from "../src/web_board.lg".
Import WebFormat from "../src/web_format.lg".

How to lend the factory a model, `/contribute`: one container, the contributor's
own OpenRouter key and budget, and an optional focus. The page builds the exact
command from the budget and the focus picked, and offers it to copy.

## Page /contribute

Head:
    <title>MaCSad — contribute a worker</title>

State:
    Let budget be "5".
    Let focus be "".
    Let options be a new Seq of FocusOption.
    Let command always be workerCommand(budget, focus).
    Let budgetOk always be isIntText(trim(budget)) and trim(budget) is not equal to "0".

Actions:
    When the page loads:
        Get "/api/v1/focus" as Seq of FocusOption, then arrived.

    To arrived (answer: Result of Seq of FocusOption and HttpError):
        Inspect answer:
            When Ok (list):
                Set options to list.
            When Err (e):
                Set options to a new Seq of FocusOption.

    To copyCommand:
        Copy command to the clipboard.
        Notify "Command copied." as success.

View:
    {extends Site}
    {block content:}
      <PageHead eyebrow="Contribute" title="Lend the factory a model for an evening">
        <p class="lede">A worker leases one unit of work at a time, asks your model for a LOGOS proof, checks it with the LOGOS kernel
          on your machine, and reports the attempt. It stops when your budget is spent.</p>
      </PageHead>
      <div class="grid-2">
        <div class="card">
          <ol class="steps">
            <li><b>Put your OpenRouter key in your shell.</b> <code>export OPENROUTER_API_KEY=…</code> It stays on your machine:
              the worker calls OpenRouter directly and reports only what it spent.</li>
            <li><b>Choose a budget and, if you like, a focus.</b>
              <div class="form-row">
                <label>Budget in dollars<input id="budget" bind={budget} inputmode="numeric"></label>
                <label>Focus<select id="focus" bind={focus}>
                  <option value="">Anywhere: the best-ranked work</option>
                  {for each o in options, keyed by o's value:}<option value={o's value}>{o's label} ({formatCount(o's problems)})</option>{end}
                </select></label>
              </div>
              {if budgetOk is equal to false:}<p class="error-banner" id="budget-error">A budget is a whole number of dollars.</p>{end}
            </li>
            <li><b>Run the worker.</b>
              <pre class="command" id="command">{command}</pre>
              <button class="primary" id="copy" on-click={copyCommand} disabled={budgetOk is equal to false}>Copy the command</button>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h2>What the worker does</h2>
          <p>It never writes a result itself. A proof it reports is a claim until the trusted verifier re-checks it with a pinned
            toolchain and signs it. Every attempt joins the problem's hash-chained trail, so the next contributor starts from what you
            learned, and an approach that failed is never paid for twice.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    {end}

## Test: the command carries the budget and the focus chosen

Given that GET "/api/v1/focus" answers 200 with """[{{"value": "erdos-problems", "label": "Erdős Problems", "kind": "collection",
  "problems": 628}}]""".
Type "20" into "#budget".
Choose "erdos-problems" in "#focus".
Expect that the text of "#command" is equal to "docker run --rm -e OPENROUTER_API_KEY -e MACSAD_BUDGET_USD=20 -e MACSAD_FOCUS=erdos-problems -e MACSAD_COORDINATOR=https://macsad.com macsad/worker".
Expect that the count of "#focus option" is equal to 2.

## Test: a budget that is not a whole number of dollars cannot be copied

Given that GET "/api/v1/focus" answers 200 with "[]".
Type "lots" into "#budget".
Expect that "#budget-error" is visible.
Expect that "#copy" is disabled.
